  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-archive-manager-plus",
      "text": "Delete DeepSeek Harness sessions from the session menu, or manage archived sessions in Settings. Deletion removes the session log and related records; archiving alone only hides the session.\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-archive-manager-plus)\n[](https://github.com/MS666666/dsh-archive-manager)\n[](LICENSE)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "**Plugin 0.1.10 targets DeepSeek Harness v0.2.2-rc.1.** It uses the new native context-menu service and handles the updated session publication states. The legacy v0.2.1-rc.5 menu fallback remains, but the full runtime checks for this release target v0.2.2-rc.1."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "The unchanged runtime code passed **20 tests** in 0.1.8, including three integration tests using pinned official Harness components. They cover native menu registration, stopping an active Agent turn, workspace synchronization, plain and zstd log deletion, projection-cache cleanup, and recreating the host from persisted data. Other sessions and historical cost records are preserved."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "**Desktop version manually verified:** on November 6, 2026, desktop session deletion was verified with 0.1.8 and confirmed to work normally. Version 0.1.10 updates documentation and package metadata only; runtime code is unchanged. Session teardown uses version-specific host internals, so compatibility with other Harness versions is not assumed. See the [compatibility report](https://github.com/MS666666/dsh-archive-manager/blob/main/docs/compatibility-0.2.2-rc.1.md) for the exact scope and reproduction steps."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- **Delete session** in the session row's `⋯` menu, with confirmation before any change.\n- **Settings → Archive Manager**: list archived sessions with their title, creation time, and log availability; restore or permanently delete them.\n- Stop running work and release the session's writer and in-memory state before deleting its log.\n- Remove workspace membership and notify the native sidebar session feed.\n- Keep persistent deletion receipts and clean up stale archive records or late cache writes that would otherwise bring deleted entries back.\n- Require same-origin POST requests and validate session IDs before filesystem operations."
    },
    {
      "section": "Add Plugin — recommended",
      "text": "1. Open DeepSeek Harness → **Settings → Plugins → Add Plugin**. Depending on the UI locale, plugin management may also be available from the sidebar.\n2. Enter the npm package spec:\n\n```text\n   dsh-archive-manager-plus@0.1.10\n   ```\n\n3. Complete installation, then fully quit Harness, including its tray process, and reopen it once to load both plugin halves."
    },
    {
      "section": "Add Plugin — recommended",
      "text": "To install the newest npm release later, enter `dsh-archive-manager-plus` or use the host's plugin update action. For a local build, enter the **absolute path** to `dsh-archive-manager-plus-0.1.10.tgz`, without surrounding quotes in the input field."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from source on Windows",
      "text": "Clone or download this repository, then run the script from its root:\n\n```powershell\npowershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\install.ps1 -DryRun\npowershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\\install.ps1\n```\n\nFor a custom Harness home:\n\n```powershell\n.\\install.ps1 -DSHHome \"D:\\path\\to\\dsh-home\" -DryRun\n.\\install.ps1 -DSHHome \"D:\\path\\to\\dsh-home\"\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from source on Windows",
      "text": "| Parameter | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `-ProfileDir <path>` | Explicit profile directory; takes priority over home detection. |\n| `-DSHHome <path>` | Explicit home, then `DSH_HOME`, then `~/.dsh`. |\n| `-ProfileName <name>` | Select a profile; otherwise detect `desktop` first, then `web`. |\n| `-DryRun` | Preview without changing files. |\n| `-SkipCopy` | Update only the profile manifest; the plugin files must already be installed. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install from source on Windows",
      "text": "The script copies the plugin files, registers its dependency and bundle, and verifies the profile manifest with Node. Manifest writes use UTF-8 without BOM. It keeps a manifest backup and restores that backup if final manifest verification fails; this does **not** provide rollback for deleted sessions."
    },
    {
      "section": "Manual profile setup",
      "text": "If the host's plugin manager is unavailable, install into the intended profile directory:\n\n```powershell\ncd \"<profile-directory>\"\nnpm install dsh-archive-manager-plus@0.1.10\n```\n\nEnsure that profile's `package.json` contains the dependency and bundle entry below. Merge them into the existing manifest; do not replace other dependencies or bundles.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"dsh-archive-manager-plus\": \"0.1.10\"\n  },"
    },
    {
      "section": "Manual profile setup",
      "text": "Save without a UTF-8 BOM, then fully quit and reopen Harness. Installing into an unrelated project directory does not activate a Harness plugin."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "**Direct deletion:** session row → `⋯` → **Delete session** → confirm. Confirmation archives the target, stops its running work, releases it, and deletes its log and related records. Canceling the dialog makes no changes.\n\n**Archive management:** open **Settings → Archive Manager**. Use **Restore** to unarchive a session without deleting its log, or **Delete** to remove it permanently after confirmation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage",
      "text": "Deletion is irreversible. If loading, publication, or saving is still in progress, the plugin may refuse deletion and show an error. If a later step fails, the session may remain archived; retry or inspect it in Archive Manager. Existing deletion receipts apply to sessions deleted by versions that recorded them; a leftover entry from an older version may need to be deleted once more."
    },
    {
      "section": "Data affected",
      "text": "Deletion releases the loaded Agent and session, closes the log writer, and removes:\n\n- The session directory under `<DSH_HOME>/sessions/<encoded-workspace>/<session-id>/`.\n- Its archive/pin markers and workspace membership through the live registry.\n- Its current per-session projection-cache record and any legacy cache entry.\n- Its cached host index entries, followed by a native sidebar removal notification."
    },
    {
      "section": "Data affected",
      "text": "The plugin records deleted IDs in `<DSH_HOME>/storages/archive-manager-deleted.json` to repair stale state or late projection-cache writes. It does not scan for and automatically delete unrelated session logs. Historical cost ledgers are not removed.\n\nDo not include credentials, usernames, machine-specific paths, or private conversation content in public issues."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development and verification",
      "text": "Requires a Node version compatible with the target Harness. Runtime verification for 0.1.8 used Node 24 and official v0.2.2-rc.1 packages.\n\n```powershell\nnpm run setup:integration\nnpm test\nnpm run test:integration\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development and verification",
      "text": "The setup command installs locked test dependencies into `.compat-runtime` inside this repository. Tests use temporary data directories and an offline model adapter; they do not touch the user's Harness home or call paid models. Without these dependencies, the three official-component integration tests are explicitly skipped; a run with skipped tests is not the full release validation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development and verification",
      "text": "`client/client.js` is a handwritten browser module bundle; `lib/` contains the host ESM modules. No build step is required. Restart the host after host-side changes.\n\nBefore publishing, run the complete tests and `npm publish --dry-run`. Publish the same version from `package.json` to npm and create the matching GitHub tag/release."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
